# Element Reactions

Status: DONE
Milestone: M2 Vertical slice
Dependencies: `02_DOMAIN_RULES.todo`, `04_TERRITORY_PAINTING.todo`

## Purpose

Make Ice, Fire, and Mist mechanically deterministic and immediately readable.

## Tasks

- [x] Create Ice and Fire element configuration.
- [x] Create Mist reaction configuration.
- [x] Implement reaction ownership/state rules.
- [x] Implement contested-reaction bank award.
- [x] Implement reaction event.
- [x] Implement visual material state.
- [x] Implement reaction VFX placeholder.
- [x] Implement reaction audio placeholder.
- [x] Define first player status interaction.
- [x] Implement status telegraph and contact-bound lifetime.
- [x] Add conversion and status tests.
- [x] Run comprehension playtest.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Players can distinguish Ice, Fire, and Mist without relying on color alone.
- [x] Reaction result is deterministic.
- [x] Visible reaction occurs at the authoritative contact.
- [x] Status effects are telegraphed and configurable.
- [x] Playtesters predict the reaction after seeing it twice.

## Completion evidence

- Started after Territory Painting completed in commit `9fe5b2a`.
- Added persistent Ice, Fire, and Mist presentation/status configuration.
- Added diagonal Ice stripes, Fire dots, and Mist crosshatch without texture assets.
- Added authoritative reaction events with contact, state, element, and bank data.
- Added a fixed six-slot reaction visual/audio feedback pool.
- Added configurable friendly boost and hostile slow with foot markers and a dedicated HUD status row.
- Validation: 24 EditMode tests and 20 PlayMode tests passed.
- First review requested selected-element HUD coloring and clearer animated/audio reaction feedback. A
  universal Mist slow was then rejected because it contradicted intended team-territory synergy.
- Replaced the Mist slow with sandbox team affinity: selected-element territory boosts to 1.40x, opposing
  primary territory slows to 0.70x, and Neutral/Mist remains 1.00x. HUD and foot markers identify the effect.
- Isolated terrain status into its own HUD row. Friendly boost uses selected-team text on transparency;
  hostile slow alone uses hostile-terrain background with selected-team foreground.
- Screenshot review found status overlap, a hidden reset instruction, and an oversized fixed background.
  Moved the row below the debug block and made its width content-driven with compact padding.
- Developer approved the corrected affinity behavior and final isolated HUD layout.
- Final validation: 24/24 EditMode tests, 20/20 PlayMode tests, and Windows development build passed.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-28 - Began implementation after the developer approved and committed Territory Painting.
- 2026-08-28 - Completed after iterative hands-on review approved reaction readability, territory synergy,
  movement telegraphs, and final HUD layout.
